Vikram and Betal: The Careless Worker (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100134

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a worker who always rushed through his work,” said Betal. “He never paid attention to details.”

One day, his master gave him an important task.

The worker quickly finished it without checking.

But he made many mistakes.

Another worker took his time and did the same task carefully.

His work was perfect.

The master praised the careful worker.

The careless worker felt bad.

He asked, “Why was my work not good?”

The master said, “Because you did not do it with care.”

The worker understood his mistake.

From that day, he started working carefully.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what is the lesson here?”

Vikram replied, “Doing work carefully is better than doing it quickly.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Careful work leads to better results.
